-- title:
--   Unique discrete place centred on a maximal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field, $\rho : B \to F$ a ring homomorphism, and $\mathfrak{y} \subseteq B$ a maximal ideal with $\ker \rho \subseteq \mathfrak{y}$. Let $R$ be a subring of $F$ whose members are characterised by the condition that $x \in R$ if and only if there exist $s, t \in B$ with $t \notin \mathfrak{y}$ and $x\,\rho(t) = \rho(s)$, i.e. $R$ consists of the quotients $\rho(s)/\rho(t)$ with $t \notin \mathfrak{y}$. Assume $R$ is a discrete valuation ring and that $F$ is a field of fractions of $R$. Then there is a valuation subring $P$ of $F$ such that: $\rho(s) \in P$ for every $s \in B$; for $s \in B$ one has $\rho(s)$ in the set of nonunits of $P$ (its maximal ideal) exactly when $s \in \mathfrak{y}$; any valuation subring $P'$ of $F$ with these same two properties equals $P$; every element $e$ of $P$ satisfies $e - \rho(s) \in P.\mathrm{nonunits}$ for some $s \in B$, so that $\rho(B)$ attains every residue of $P$; and $P$ is a principal ideal ring.
--
--   This is the standard dictionary between the local-ring and the place-theoretic descriptions of a closed point: a localisation of $B$ at a maximal ideal which happens to be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $F$ is the unique valuation subring of $F$ dominating $\rho(B)$ and centred on $\mathfrak{y}$, and its residue field is already generated by the image of $B$. It is used for the local ring of a modular curve at a closed point, in the construction of a valuation subring with prescribed residue behaviour on an integral model of $X_1(N)/X_0(p)$-type charts.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_unique_centred_of_isDiscreteValuationRing_of_isFractionRing.lean

